Building csmake packages from a checkout
========================================

Debian / Ubuntu
---------------
The Debian packager ships with csmake core, so a bare checkout is enough:

    ./csmake clean package

The .deb lands in target/.

See:
    ./csmake --list-phases
    ./csmake --list-commands
for more help.


Non-Debian platforms (macOS, RPM, signed packages)
--------------------------------------------------
The other packagers live in two sibling libraries:

    csmake-packaging - RpmPackage, HomebrewFormula, HomebrewBottle,
                       HomebrewCask, ApplePackage, WheelPackage, ...
    csmake-swak      - Signature, AsciiGPGSignature (needed for the
                       'signed' command), and other helpers

Clone them next to this checkout:

    git clone https://github.com/devops-csmake/csmake-swak
    git clone https://github.com/devops-csmake/csmake-packaging

and put them on the modules path when you build.  NOTE the leading ':' --
it appends to the default search path ('+local:+path'); without it the
default path (and with it csmake's own core modules) is replaced:

    ./csmake --modules-path=':../csmake-swak:../csmake-packaging' \
        --command=<packaging-command> clean package

Packaging commands defined in this csmakefile:

    homebrew-only    - Homebrew formula (.rb) + source tarball
    homebrew-bottle  - Homebrew bottle archive + formula
    homebrew-cask    - Homebrew cask wrapping the .pkg installer
    apple-only       - macOS .pkg installer
    signed           - signed .deb and .rpm (also needs GPG keys)

Results land under target/ (e.g. target/homebrew/, target/applepkg/).

Installing the Homebrew build locally
-------------------------------------
Current Homebrew requires formulae to live in a tap; standalone .rb
files are rejected.  One-time setup:

    brew tap-new devops-csmake/local --no-git

Then after each build:

    cp target/homebrew/csmake.rb \
       "$(brew --repository)/Library/Taps/devops-csmake/homebrew-local/Formula/"
    brew install devops-csmake/local/csmake     (or: brew reinstall)

The generated formula's url points at the local tarball (file://...), so
no network hosting is needed for a local install.

Module autoloading (where this is headed)
-----------------------------------------
csmake can lazily download module libraries from the csmake-registry
(https://github.com/devops-csmake/csmake-registry) into ~/.csmake/modules
when a section type is not found locally.  Once csmake-swak and
csmake-packaging publish .csm releases to the registry, the
--modules-path wiring above becomes unnecessary: a bare csmake install
resolves the packaging modules on first use, on any platform.


Testing
-------
    ./csmake --command=test test

runs the unit test suite (file tracking, csmake modules, secrets,
module docs, launcher bootstrap).  RUNTESTS.sh runs the full spec-test
suite (Linux; requires python coverage).
